  bodyName: Venus
  classification: Terrestrial Planet
  positionFromSun: 2nd Planet
  overview: Venus is the second planet from the Sun. It has an extremely dense carbon
    dioxide atmosphere that produces a powerful greenhouse effect. Its surface is
    dominated by volcanic features mountains and extensive plains.
  keyCharacteristics: 'Hottest planetary surface in the Solar System.

    Extremely
    dense carbon dioxide atmosphere.

    Retrograde rotation.

    Thick sulfuric
    acid cloud layers.

    Surface pressure approximately 92 times Earth''s.

    No
    known natural satellites.'
  meanRadiusKm: 6051.8
  meanDiameterKm: 12103.6
